KZ3 patch 5005: cellFont outline API on real fonts (system fontset), the RE notes s.11.
KZ3 opens one system font (cellFontOpenFontset type 0x109) and reads glyph outlines through cellFontGetCharGlyphMetrics,
cellFontGenerateCharGlyph and cellFontDeleteGlyph (NIDs 0xD8EAEE9F, 0xC17259DE, 0xD62F5D76); the library defined none of them, so
the imports took the unresolved-NID path (CELL_OK, out-parameters untouched) and every Cyrillic, Hangul, kana and Han glyph was blank.
New libs/font/cellFontOutline.c: a font chain per fontset handle, the player's own firmware fonts first ($KZ3_FONT_DIR/SCE-PS3-*.TTF),
then bundled Noto (SIL OFL) from $KZ3_FONT_FALLBACK_DIR, <exe dir>/fonts or ./fonts, chosen per code point by cmap lookup; CJK order
by $KZ3_FONT_HAN (jp default, kr, sc, tc) or kz3_font_set_han_pref(). Outlines are written in the guest CellFontGlyph layout the game's
converter reads (metrics at +0x08, h_advance at +0x18, s16 contour and point counts at +0x28/+0x2A, float x,y pairs, u8 on/off flags,
u16 contour end indexes), in pixels at the font's scale, from a library-owned guest pool (4 MiB, size-class free lists) that sys_memory_alloc_window (patch 1113) takes from the mapper range, so no title reservation can be handed the same pages (was a fixed 0xB8000000 inside v0.17.0's mapper range, SPU pass 97).
CFF cubics are split into quadratics (the game's converter is TrueType-style). cellFontSetScalePixel takes its floats from f1/f2 through a
context handler (the flat integer-register adapter passed garbage), also for cellFontSetupRenderScalePixel. cellFontEndLibrary is added.
No decryption, no PUP reading: the files are used as they are. Fonts are never committed. Host test: tools/assets/test_font5005.sh.
Upstream candidate (general cellFont: outline API, fontset backed by real files, SetScalePixel float arguments).

